# Ryoku base package set. One package per line; '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# The installer (installation/backend/ryoku-install) pacstraps this whole set.
# Per-profile GPU drivers and CPU microcode come from hardware.packages.

# Core system
base
base-devel
# rust: the depth cutout worker and several AUR dependencies are Rust
# programs, so the toolchain is part of the base set (not the optional dev
# toolchains in dev.packages), and every Ryoku machine can always build them.
rust
linux
linux-firmware
# linux-headers + dkms: the shipped kernel's headers and the DKMS build system,
# so out-of-tree driver modules build (e.g. xpadneo-dkms, the Xbox One/Series
# Bluetooth pads; see aur.packages). ryoku-desktop hard-depends on both, and a
# DKMS module fails to build without matching headers. The CachyOS kernel is an
# opt-in post-install (the CachyOS Layer extras bundle), never baked into the
# base, so the base ships and boots the stock linux kernel.
linux-headers
dkms
mkinitcpio
sudo

# Boot chain
btrfs-progs
cryptsetup
dosfstools
efibootmgr
limine
# limine-entry-tool stack ([ryoku]): the hook regenerates the menu, detects other
# OSes (FIND_BOOTLOADERS), builds the UKI tree; sync adds the Snapshots submenu.
limine-mkinitcpio-hook
limine-snapper-sync
plymouth
snapper
# snap-pac: automatic pre/post snapshots around pacman transactions, wired to the
# snapper "root" config by the installer.
snap-pac

# Networking
networkmanager
iwd
# wpa_supplicant: the alternate NetworkManager Wi-Fi backend. iwd stays the
# default, but its WPA3-SAE support is incomplete (WPA3 / mixed networks like
# Android phone hotspots fail to associate); Settings -> Connections can flip
# the backend to this one via ryoku-wifi-backend.
wpa_supplicant
# wireless-regdb: regulatory database; without it the WiFi domain caps at world-00 (low TX power)
wireless-regdb
# iw: ryoku-wifi-powersave (Game Mode) disables 802.11 power-save for low latency
iw
# nftables: fail-closed firewall backing the Connections kill switch. The helper
# drops all non-loopback IPv4/IPv6 traffic before it asks NetworkManager to
# deactivate managed interfaces.
nftables

# Bluetooth (BlueZ). bluetoothd is the org.bluez D-Bus daemon the shell and hub
# Bluetooth UIs (Quickshell.Bluetooth) talk to; bluez-utils ships bluetoothctl,
# which the pair-trust-connect flows shell out to. The installer enables
# bluetooth.service (see installation/backend/lib/bootloader.sh).
bluez
bluez-utils

# Audio (PipeWire)
pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
# pipewire-audio pulls the Bluetooth A2DP codec libraries (LDAC, AAC, aptX via
# libfreeaptx, LC3) as hard deps. Without it a fresh install has only the SBC
# fallback, so headsets sound muffled and 51-ryoku-bluetooth.conf's codec list
# has nothing to select. (libopenaptx was dropped from the repos; libfreeaptx
# is its successor and rides in here.)
pipewire-audio
# alsa-utils: alsamixer / amixer / alsactl, the standard tools for inspecting and
# unsticking a muted hardware codec by hand. Not used by the desktop at runtime
# (PipeWire owns volume on stock defaults); shipped so audio stays diagnosable, as
# omarchy's base set does too.
alsa-utils
# rtkit: RealtimeKit grants PipeWire/WirePlumber realtime scheduling priority.
# base set so the installer's rtkit-daemon.service enable succeeds even offline
# (it otherwise arrives only with the ryoku-desktop umbrella).
rtkit

# Graphics base (vendor drivers added per profile)
mesa
vulkan-icd-loader

# Desktop runtime: Xwayland, the GTK portal, and the Qt/GTK stack. The
# compositor, its portal backend, and its polkit agent are compositor-specific
# and ship with the compositor meta-package.
# SDDM may still be built with Qt5; the greeter's native Wayland QPA plugin is
# version-specific, so qt6-wayland alone cannot start it.
xorg-xwayland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-user-dirs
qt6-wayland
qt5-wayland
qt6ct
adwaita-icon-theme
# gnome-themes-extra ships the standalone Adwaita-dark GTK theme the Hyprland
# autostart selects (gsettings gtk-theme). Without it that name resolves to
# nothing on disk and GTK3 apps -- notably the xdg-desktop-portal-gtk file
# chooser -- fall back to the built-in light Adwaita in a dark session.
gnome-themes-extra
# Papirus-Dark is the shipped Qt icon theme (ryoku/shell/qt6ct/qt6ct.conf); it
# covers named freedesktop icons (e.g. network-wired) that Adwaita ships only as
# -symbolic, so the launcher's all-apps grid resolves every entry's logo.
papirus-icon-theme

# Cursor theme from the official repo (the rest of the Ryoku cursor set is AUR,
# see aur.packages). vimix is a modern flat XCursor theme.
vimix-cursors

# Flatpak: the stash file drop installs .flatpak bundles, and it is the portable
# app channel alongside the [ryoku] and Arch repos.
flatpak

# Login + lockscreen (SDDM greeter + qylock clockwork)
sddm
# weston: the SDDM greeter's Wayland compositor (weston --shell=kiosk). Running
# the greeter on Wayland like the Hyprland session lets SDDM tear it down at
# login; the old X11 greeter was orphaned when a Wayland session started and
# kept drawing power. A Wayland greeter cannot start without it. See
# ryoku/lockscreen/sddm/setup.
weston
polkit
gnome-keyring
qt6-declarative
qt6-5compat
qt6-svg
qt6-multimedia
qt6-multimedia-ffmpeg
gst-plugins-base
gst-plugins-good
gst-plugins-bad
gst-plugins-ugly
# gst-libav rounds out GStreamer codec coverage (via ffmpeg) for media that
# gst-plugins-{good,bad} cannot demux or decode on their own.
gst-libav

# Wayland tools
# matugen: the material-you palette engine the shell daemon runs on every
# wallpaper / scheme change to author colors.json and fan it into app configs.
matugen
brightnessctl
hypridle
upower
power-profiles-daemon
fuzzel
grim
playerctl
slurp
wl-clipboard
wl-clip-persist

# Applications
chromium
# firefox: the second browser, shipped so a Gecko engine is always on hand for a
# site Chromium renders badly. It does not become the default: the `browser` role
# in ryoku/shell/scripts/ryoku-app stays chromium, and Ryoku Settings ->
# App Overrides is where a user repoints the launcher key.
firefox
kitty
mpv
mpv-mpris
nautilus
# nautilus-python: runs the Ryoku stash actions in the file-manager right-click menu
nautilus-python

# Virtual machines (Ryoku Settings > GPU > Machine): a windowed VM runs in QEMU
# on the host GPU. edk2-ovmf is the UEFI firmware and virglrenderer the host-GL
# acceleration; the optional GPU-passthrough stack (Looking Glass) installs on
# demand from Ryoku Settings.
qemu-desktop
edk2-ovmf
virglrenderer

# Containers: the runtime behind the stash "Cobalt engine" switch, which runs
# downloads through a local cobalt instance (cobalt ships only as a Docker
# image). The service is deliberately NOT enabled here: a box that never opens
# that switch should not pay for a running dockerd, a docker0 bridge and its
# iptables rules. `ryoku-docker provision`, which the setup wizard drives,
# enables it on first use. No docker-compose: the cobalt lifecycle is a single
# `docker run` (ryoku/hyprland/scripts/stash-cobalt-server.sh).
docker

# Gaming (Bazzite-style stack): gamescope is a nested micro-compositor that runs
# a game isolated from the desktop, bypassing the XWayland compositing that is
# the real source of in-game and Steam-overlay lag on Wayland (run a title with
# `gamescope -f -- %command%` in Steam's launch options). gamemode (feral) is the
# perf governor Steam/Lutris invoke via `gamemoderun %command%`. mangohud is the
# FPS/frametime overlay (via gamescope's `--mangoapp`). 64-bit here; the lib32
# variants for 32-bit titles ride the opt-in multilib set.
gamescope
gamemode
mangohud

# Game controllers. Most of the work is already in the kernel and needs nothing
# here: hid_playstation and hid_sony cover DualSense and DualShock, hid_nintendo
# covers Switch Pro, and xpad covers wired Xbox pads plus every XInput off-brand
# (Turtle Beach included, matched by vendor + interface signature since 6.4, so
# no per-brand driver exists to add). The gap the kernel leaves is Bluetooth:
# xpad does not speak it, so a wireless Xbox pad needs xpadneo, and these pads
# also need L2CAP ERTM off to pair at all (99-ryoku-controller.conf).
#
# xpadneo ships from [ryoku] rather than the AUR so `ryoku update` can install
# and update it; see release/packages/xpadneo-dkms.
#
# game-devices-udev is the other half, and it is not a driver: the kernel binds
# these pads but does not grant userspace access to them, so without its rules a
# pad that works as a gamepad still reports no battery and cannot be configured
# by Steam or an emulator. 27 vendors, which is most of what people own once they
# stray from first-party pads: 8BitDo, PowerA, PDP, Nacon, Hori, Mad Catz,
# Razer, Thrustmaster, Valve. Also moved out of the AUR, for the same reason.
#
# The Xbox Wireless Dongle is deliberately NOT here: its driver (xone) ships
# `blacklist xpad`, which would take wired and off-brand pads down with it. It is
# an opt-in install instead.
xpadneo-dkms
game-devices-udev

# Bluetooth adapter firmware. linux-firmware's default set already pulls
# -intel, -realtek, -mediatek, -atheros and -broadcom, which covers essentially
# every built-in and USB adapter. The one hole it leaves is Broadcom's .hcd
# patchram blobs (linux-firmware-broadcom ships 118 files and zero .hcd), and
# without the matching .hcd a BCM20702/BCM43142 dongle enumerates and then never
# comes up: "Patch brcm/BCM20702A1-....hcd not found".
broadcom-bt-firmware

# Shell + CLI
bash-completion
blesh
bat
btop
eza
fastfetch
fd
fish
fzf
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-history-substring-search
zsh-syntax-highlighting
git
github-cli
lazygit
neovim
# pciutils: lspci is the primary GPU-detection path for the per-profile driver
# scripts during pacstrap (system/hardware/drivers/*.sh); absent from the chroot otherwise.
pciutils
ripgrep
starship
zoxide

# Ryoku shell (quickshell desktop), its runtime helpers, and the yazi file manager
quickshell
cava
cliphist
hyprpicker
imagemagick
# waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan: GPU AI upscaler behind ryoshot Beautify's HD export and
# ryowalls Enhance. official repo, in the base set so every install ships it.
waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan
jq
openrgb
# external-monitor brightness for the pill mixer's DISPLAY faders, over DDC/CI
ddcutil
yazi

# File stash + weather: LocalSend, AppImage/tar install, ffmpeg compress,
# yt-dlp download, and file-open integration for the pill
curl
libnotify
python
xdg-utils
ffmpeg
yt-dlp
desktop-file-utils

# Launcher (command palette, Super+Space): qalc backs the calculator (units,
# currency, %, functions; a Python arithmetic fallback covers a qalc-less box),
# and songrec powers Recognize Music.
libqalculate
songrec

# Screen toolkit (pill Super+D): OCR text recognition (tesseract) and QR scanning
# (zbar). The lens, color picker, and webcam mirror reuse curl/jq/grim/slurp,
# hyprpicker, and mpv from above.
tesseract
tesseract-data-eng
zbar

# Screen recorder (pill Super+U utilities): gpu-screen-recorder, with a
# wf-recorder fallback for multi-GPU machines, driven by ryoku-cmd-screenrecord.
gpu-screen-recorder
wf-recorder

# Voice dictation (pill Super+`, Voxtype from voxtype-bin): wtype types the
# transcription into the focused app on Wayland.
wtype

# Fonts
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-cjk
inter-font
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
ttf-firacode-nerd
ttf-hack-nerd
ttf-material-symbols-variable
# otf-space-grotesk: the Space Grotesk UI sans the shell/Hub render for the brand
# type stack. Ships from [ryoku] (release/packages/otf-space-grotesk), built from
# the upstream prebuilt OTF release, so it is pacstrapped on every install and
# kept current by `ryoku update`. Its AUR pkgbase builds with fontforge and could
# not bake headless in the ISO CI, so it lives here as a reliable repo package.
otf-space-grotesk
# ttf-maple-mono-nf: Maple Mono (Nerd Font) monospace face offered for the
# terminal and code. Ships from [ryoku] (release/packages/ttf-maple-mono-nf) as
# the upstream prebuilt NF release, so it pacstraps on install and updates with
# `ryoku update`; same reliable model as otf-space-grotesk.
ttf-maple-mono-nf
